# The user-global excludes file (~/.config/git/ignore) treats .agents/ as local
# tooling. In this repository it is a REQUIRED artifact: scripts/check-structure.py
# demands .agents/ and .agents/AGENTS.md, so excluding it makes CI verify a tree
# the author never had — the gate passes locally and fails in CI for a reason
# invisible from the working copy.
#
# Same defect, same line of the same global ignore file, previously recorded as
# NR-scms-002 in semantic-cms. Re-include the operating contract; the generated
# corpora under .agents/ stay ignored by the `llms*` rule above.
!.agents/
!.agents/AGENTS.md
